  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1916c2a94225-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Rehnquist, the central issue is whether the United States Postal Service qualifies as a \u201cperson\u201d under the Sherman Act and related antitrust statutes."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States Postal Service",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1916c2a94225-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States Postal Service, the Ninth Circuit previously held that the Postal Service may be sued for treble damages under federal antitrust law, but the petitioner argues that holding was erroneous."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1916c2a94225-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1916c2a94225-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The respondent contends that Congress authorized the Postal Service to compete commercially, making it a \u201cperson\u201d for antitrust purposes."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "United States Postal Service",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 9,
                "start": 9
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States Postal Service, the Postal Service is not a \u201cperson\u201d under antitrust law."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States Postal Service",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States Postal Service, the Ninth Circuit\u2019s holding that the Postal Service may be sued for treble damages was erroneous."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "United States Postal Service",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 11,
                "start": 11
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to United States Postal Service, the Postal Service may sue and be sued in its official name."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 53,
                "start": 53
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, congress treats the Postal Service as a federal entity subject to statutes such as the FOIA, Privacy Act, and Title\u202fVII, not as a private corporation."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner \u2013 United States Postal Service",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondents",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondents, congress launched the Postal Service into the commercial world, authorizing it to compete and thus making it a \u201cperson\u201d under antitrust law for several reasons."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondents",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondents, the Postal Service contains a \u201csue\u2011and\u2011be\u2011sued\u201d clause that distinguishes it from cases lacking such a clause."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Krent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 36,
                "start": 36
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Krent, public corporations, states, and foreign governmental entities have been treated as \u201cpersons\u201d under antitrust law; the Postal Service should similarly qualify."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Krent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1916c2a942259dfa051f76a8fe12dfc99f335530550c6c9a23772c06c78e05fe",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1916c2a94225-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 50,
                "start": 50
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Krent, historical case law under the Lanham Act suggests the Postal Service can be considered a \u201cperson.\u201d"
        }
      ],
